{
  "id": "COMPOUND:1727 - PROTEIN:5840",
  "verbalization": "Castanospermine is implicated in the interaction with H9 through a multi-step mechanism involving a sialyltransferase enzyme. The evidence suggests that Castanospermine targets CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which is a key enzyme in the synthesis of sialic acid. This enzyme is subsequently targeted by (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan, a compound that is known to interact with the sialyltransferase. The same sialyltransferase is also targeted by Mycalamide D, another compound that has been shown to interact with H9. This indicates that the sialyltransferase is a common target across multiple compounds, and that H9 is a downstream effector of these interactions. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of the sialyltransferase in mediating the effects of Castanospermine and related compounds on H9, suggesting a potential mechanism by which these compounds influence cellular processes through the modulation of sialic acid synthesis.",
